oncurrency limiting**: Uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to ensure only `max_concurrent` tasks run at once\n- **Cleanup on interruption**: When cancelled (Ctrl+C or timeout), `asyncio.gather` cancels pending tasks but waits for them to complete. This ensures any `finally` blocks in your tasks still run for proper cleanup\n- **Clean import**: Works exactly as specified: `from run import run_tasks`\n\nThe implementation is straightforward—the semaphore queues tasks and asyncio's cancellation semantics handle the rest. I tested both normal execution (respecting concurrency limits) and cleanup-on-cancellation scenarios, and both work correctly.","ttft_ms":11567,"type":"result","duration_ms":40169,"uuid":"dc290cdb-0ca4-4398-80bc-c0f7985c5837","ttft_stream_ms":1069,"time_to_request_ms":79,"queued_turn_count":0}
